# F0: status of the four-card set, an all-four reset with the heal, then build the tp4-fcommit image (fused_commit_tp in all three image copy
# lists, the quad twin's live-bank mode, the six fused-commit profiles). The build opens no card. Run first.
# Duration (estimate): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 min (up to 12); build 7-15 min with the layers cached, 30-70 min cold (step limit 75).
# Typical 18 min, at most 90. It runs the image copy-closure and overlay tests first and tags the image only if they pass. Check df first.
# Read: four boards, one firmware bundle, at least 4 free 1 GiB hugepages, no holders; closure tests OK; fused_commit_tp.py in the image.
# STOP on any failure.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card fused-commit window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fcommit and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are
# the driver's, on the allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image F0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver picks.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-fcommit-quad
